{
  "name": "agent_send",
  "description": "Send a message to an agent as the user would type it; queued while it works. Only send what the user asked for. A stopped agent takes no plain message. Only a recorded non-user stop (idle, task completion, restart) permits resume; user and unknown stops need the user's Resume. If the next work needs its context (investigation followed by a fix, rework, the user asked for this agent), send with resume and resume_why: the same session and permission mode, your text first, the reason shown to the user. It must be supervised (give task unless it is on an open task of yours). A nearly full one is compacted first. Unrelated work or one off track: agent_start anew (agent_read the old). Unsure: ask_user. A failed resume says why. A user's branch that never ran is started by its first message. Only /exit or /quit stops a running agent (tab kept); finished tasks' agents stop automatically. /exit to another conversation's task is refused (the user can close it, or agent_archive with close).\n\nA dialog holding its terminal refuses the send (dialog_open) with its first line and whether Enter alone closes it; then send with dismiss_notice true. Confirmations, permissions and pickers are never closed for you: tell the user or use interaction_answer.\n\nTo give a running agent new work, pass task from main. A successful send creates a supervised task like agent_supervise (todo with text as notes, done_when, card, 督办, task_review). Include criteria in text: the agent reads only that. One of your tasks accepts more under the same title and updates done_when. A different title, the user's own todo or another conversation's task is refused before sending. Failed sends make no task. Omit task or use null for replies, nudges or decisions. Blank fields count as omitted.\n\n`wait_seconds` observes up to 50 seconds after dispatch, appending `Inline observation` JSON: `completed`(this input's `reply`), `question`(pending `interaction_id`), `timeout`/`cancelled`/`unavailable`/`interrupted`/`failed`, with known input/session ids. Observation never answers questions, accepts tasks, resends or cancels work; normal supervision/`task_review` applies. Older nodes may time out rather than return an unrelated reply.",
  "input_schema": {
    "type": "object",
    "required": [
      "machine",
      "session_id",
      "text"
    ],
    "properties": {
      "wait_seconds": {
        "type": "integer",
        "minimum": 0,
        "description": "0/omitted: normal receipt"
      },
      "machine": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "session_id": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "text": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "inbox_item": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Inbox ID; for this conversation's eligible handoffs, omit for one, specify for several."
      },
      "resume": {
        "type": "boolean",
        "description": "resume this stopped agent with its context, text as its first message"
      },
      "resume_why": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "shown to the user"
      },
      "dismiss_notice": {
        "type": "boolean",
        "description": "Press Enter first to close a notice that only says \"Enter to continue\" (no options). Any other dialog still refuses the send."
      },
      "attachments": {
        "type": "array",
        "maxItems": 8,
        "items": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "description": "absolute paths of pictures/files the user gave in this conversation (Claude Code path or app attachment); copied to the agent, appended to its message with mentions updated; others refused"
      },
      "task": {
        "type": [
          "object",
          "null"
        ],
        "description": "new work: make it your supervised task first (main conversation only); null for a reply",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "title": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "the task in a short line (Chinese, under 20 characters)"
          },
          "done_when": {
            "type": "array",
            "maxItems": 6,
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "description": "results you can check when it says it is done (a PR merged, a sheet's link, what the live system answers)"
          },
          "expect_minutes": {
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "how long it should take from now; longer without progress counts as stuck"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
